  "dom_id": "step-q162675",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{t}{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}-t \\\\ \\sqrt{1-t}\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\frac{t}{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of ${t}^{3}-t$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{1-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,1].$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/daf03cb538fcc1546f64896cc6489beae084880feec565229e05e3db1e92b050.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,1].$",
